  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "eda-interpretation",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Interpretation\n",
    "\n",
    "- Mean overall AI literacy is 3.57 on the original 1–5 scale (SD = 0.42). AI literacy is not standardized in this descriptive table.\n",
    "\n",
    "- The SES-index mean is effectively zero by design because all seven SES items are standardized using the pooled 232-person means and SDs *after merging*, and the item z-scores are then averaged. \n",
    "\n",
    "- The SES-index SD is 0.57 rather than 1.00 because it is the mean of seven correlated item z-scores; the composite itself is not re-standardized here. The regression function subsequently standardizes the final SES index and AI outcome when reporting standardized β.\n",
    "\n",
    "- SES ingredients have moderate internal consistency (Cronbach's α = 0.687). This is close to the commonly used 0.70 threshold and is reasonable for a multidimensional SES index construct.\n",
    "\n",
    "- AI-literacy items have low internal consistency (α = 0.504). The items appear to cover heterogeneous conceptual-knowledge and ability/confidence domains rather than one interchangeable item set. \n",
    "\n",
    "-----"
   ]
  },
