    "df_ses = add_ses_space_house_variables(df)\n",
    "ses_efa_items = list(SES_EFA_ITEMS_2DIM)\n",
    "ses_diag, ses_kmo = efa_diagnostics(df_ses, 'Combined', ses_efa_items)\n",
    "ses_eigenvalues = run_scree_analysis(df_ses, 'Combined', ses_efa_items)\n",
    "ses_fa, ses_complete, ses_loadings, ses_variance = fit_efa(\n",
    "    df_ses, 'Combined', ses_efa_items, n_factors=2, rotation='oblimin'\n",
    ")\n",
    "display(ses_diag)\n",
    "display(ses_eigenvalues)\n",
    "display(ses_variance)\n",
    "_ = ses_fa.transform(ses_complete)\n",
    "ses_score_weights = pd.DataFrame(\n",
    "    ses_fa.weights_, index=ses_efa_items, columns=['SES factor 1', 'SES factor 2']\n",
    ")\n",
    "display(ses_score_weights)\n",
    "plot_loading_heatmap(ses_loadings, cutoff=.30, title='Combined SES factor loadings')"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "ses-efa-interpretation",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### SES EFA interpretation\n",
    "\n",
    "- Bartlett's test is significant and the KMO is 0.728, providing better support for the SES factor analysis than for the AI-literacy factor analysis.\n",
    "\n",
    "- Two eigenvalues exceed 1, and the two retained factors explain 40.0% of the SES-item variance.\n",
    "\n",
    "- The two scores summarize related family/institutional and material-resource dimensions.\n",
    "\n",
    "- These factor scores are not equal-weighted averages. Each observed SES variable is standardized, then multiplied by the displayed factor-score weight for each dimension. The weighted values are summed for each respondent. With oblimin rotation, the two factors are allowed to correlate.\n",
    "\n",
    "- The weights are estimated from the pooled correlation structure using minimum-residual EFA. Their signs and magnitudes determine how strongly each SES variable contributes to each factor score."
    "-----"
   ]
  },
