   "source": [
    "retained_mediator_names = ['practical_ai_use', 'language_load', 'epistemic_stance']\n",
    "retained_mediators = [f'{name}_score' for name in retained_mediator_names]\n",
    "mediator_reliability = mediator_reliability_table(df, mediator_map)\n",
    "mediator_reliability = mediator_reliability[\n",
    "    mediator_reliability['mediator'].isin(retained_mediator_names)\n",
    "]\n",
    "display(mediator_reliability)\n",
    "\n",
    "df_med = add_mediator_composites(df, mediator_map)\n",
    "df_analysis = add_ses_ai_factor_scores(\n",
    "    df_base=df_med, ai_df=df, ai_items=ai_efa_items, ai_fa=ai_fa,\n",
    "    ses_df=df_ses, ses_items=ses_efa_items, ses_fa=ses_fa,\n",
    ")\n",
    "df_analysis.to_csv('datasets/df_analysis_phase_I_combined.csv', index=False)\n",
    "\n",
    "mediation_results = run_all_simple_mediations(\n",
    "    df_analysis,\n",
    "    x=['ses_factor1_score', 'ses_factor2_score'],\n",
    "    mediators=retained_mediators,\n",
    "    outcomes=['ai_factor1_score', 'ai_factor2_score'],\n",
    "    sample_list=['Combined'],\n",
    "    n_boot=5000, seed=2026,\n",
    ")\n",
    "mediation_results['p_fdr'] = multipletests(\n",
    "    mediation_results['p_indirect_boot'], method='fdr_bh'\n",
    ")[1]\n",
    "mediation_results['p_holm'] = multipletests(\n",
    "    mediation_results['p_indirect_boot'], method='holm'\n",
    ")[1]\n",
    "mediation_results.to_csv('datasets/mediation_results_phase_I_combined.csv', index=False)\n",
    "mediation_correction_summary = pd.DataFrame({\n",
    "    'method': ['Benjamini-Hochberg FDR', 'Holm family-wise error'],\n",
    "    'significant_models': [\n",
    "        int((mediation_results['p_fdr'] < .05).sum()),\n",
    "        int((mediation_results['p_holm'] < .05).sum()),\n",
    "    ],\n",
    "    'smallest_adjusted_p': [\n",
    "        mediation_results['p_fdr'].min(),\n",
    "        mediation_results['p_holm'].min(),\n",
    "    ],\n",
    "})\n",
    "display(mediation_correction_summary)\n",
    "display(mediation_results.sort_values('p_indirect_boot').head(10))\n",
    "plot_indirect_effect_forest(mediation_results, sample='Combined')"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "mediation-interpretation",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Interpretation\n",
    "\n",
    "- Language load is the strongest two-item mediator scale (ρ = 0.578, α = 0.737). Practical AI use and learning ecology have weaker reliability.\n",
    "\n",
    "- Two pathways have unadjusted bootstrap p-values below 0.05, but none of the 20 indirect effects survives Benjamini–Hochberg correction (smallest adjusted p = 0.347) or Holm correction (smallest adjusted p = 0.573).\n",
    "\n",
    "- Accordingly, the pooled data do not provide multiplicity-adjusted evidence that any measured mediator transmits an SES effect to either AI-literacy factor.\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "network-heading",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 6. Partial-correlation network\n",
    "\n",
    "Edges represent conditional associations after controlling for every other variable in the network. Benjamini-Hochberg FDR is the primary exploratory correction, with Holm family-wise error correction shown as a stricter sensitivity analysis. Edges are not causal effects."
   ]
  },
