  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "network-interpretation",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Interpretation\n",
    "\n",
    "- Benjamini–Hochberg FDR retains 10 of the 28 possible edges. Holm's stricter family-wise error correction retains three.\n",
    "- The three Holm-robust edges are conceptual exposure–learning ecology (partial r = 0.362), language load–AI understanding (r = -0.324), and epistemic stance–AI understanding (r = 0.253).\n",
    "- Overall SES is linked to learning ecology under FDR correction (r = 0.161) but not under Holm correction, so that edge is less robust to the multiplicity assumption.\n",
    "- These are conditional associations within a cross-sectional network, not directional or causal pathways."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "hier-heading",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 7. Hierarchical regression\n",
    "\n",
    "Model 1 contains the two SES factors; Model 2 adds the three retained mediators; Model 3 adds the language-load × epistemic-stance interaction. Block tests use Holm correction and coefficient tests use FDR correction."
   ]
  },
