   "source": [
    "### Interpretation\n",
    "\n",
    "- Adding the five mediators improves explained variance for AI understanding by ΔR² = 0.183 and for AI confidence by ΔR² = 0.127; both block improvements remain significant after Holm correction.\n",
    "- The interaction block adds a smaller but statistically supported increment for AI understanding (ΔR² = 0.032, adjusted p = 0.012) and AI confidence (ΔR² = 0.034, adjusted p = 0.009).\n",
    "- In the main-effects models, language load is negatively associated with both AI outcomes, while epistemic stance is positively associated with both. Practical AI use and SES factor 2 are additionally retained for AI confidence.\n",
    "- No individual interaction coefficient survives the within-model FDR correction. The significant block tests therefore indicate joint incremental information, not a clearly isolated interaction effect."
   ]
  },
